invariant: INV-67
file: mldsa_vector.h
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh mldsa-vector
reason: the dispatch to the lanes drops its test of CH_CPU_AVX2 on
  x86-64. So the verifier runs the AVX2 lanes in every session, and the
  signer in every session with the multiply bit. A CPU without AVX2 then
  dies of SIGILL at its first transform. On a CPU with AVX2 every byte
  stays right, so no vector notices. bin/mldsa_runtime_test counts the
  calls into the lanes under each ch_cfg.cpu value and runs no AVX2
  instruction. Only an x86-64 compiler reads the line, so the script
  builds the binary for x86-64 and runs it under qemu-x86_64.

--- old
    need |= CH_CPU_AVX2;
--- new
    need |= 0;
